---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Principles from "../components/Principles.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="What Is Hakomi? | Tender of the Soul"
  ><PageHero
    eyebrow="Understanding Hakomi"
    title="Listen beneath the words."
    intro="Hakomi is a gentle, mindful, body-centered approach that follows present-moment experience with curiosity and compassion."
  />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <p class="lead">
        The body can reveal information that is not yet available to the
        conscious mind.
      </p><p>
        Rather than relying entirely on analysis or conversation, Hakomi invites
        us to notice the small, often overlooked ways experience is happening
        now: a held breath, a change in posture, an emotion at the edge of
        awareness, an impulse to move closer or pull away.
      </p><p>
        These are not problems to correct. They are doorways into the beliefs
        and organizing patterns that may be shaping how you relate, protect
        yourself, and imagine what is possible.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section soft-panel">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Four foundations</p><h2
        style="max-width:760px;margin-bottom:3rem"
      >
        A slower, kinder kind of attention.
      </h2><Principles />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What the body may communicate</p><h2>
          More than sensation.
        </h2>
      </div><div class="signals">
        {
          [
            "Breath and tension",
            "Posture and gesture",
            "Facial expression",
            "Movement and impulse",
            "Emotion and memory",
            "Repeated reactions",
            "Subtle shifts in experience",
          ].map((x) => <span>{x}</span>)
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section dark">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">The process</p><h2>
        From unconscious pattern to possibility.
      </h2><p>
        Core beliefs can quietly organize our experience. They influence what we
        expect, what we notice, and which futures feel available to us.
      </p><p>
        Through mindful contact with present-moment experience, these patterns
        may become visible. When they are safely felt and met, their charge can
        begin to soften, creating space for different choices, relationships,
        and ways of being.
      </p><p class="lead">
        When your inner architecture shifts, new possibilities become available.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow prose">
      <h2>Related ways of working</h2><p>
        Elana’s work is trauma informed and may draw from or share principles
        with mindfulness, somatic approaches, attachment-oriented work, Internal
        Family Systems-informed perspectives, and Somatic Experiencing-informed
        principles.
      </p><p>
        This language describes influences and shared principles only; it does
        not claim formal certification in these modalities. Verified training
        details will be added to the About page before publication.
      </p><h2>Is Hakomi right for me?</h2><p>
        You do not need to be comfortable with your body, good at mindfulness,
        or able to name exactly what you feel. Curiosity is enough. If you want
        a process that includes more than talking and respects your pace, Hakomi
        may offer a meaningful place to begin.
      </p><a class="button" href="/contact">Schedule a Discovery Call</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .signals {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .signals span {
    padding: 0.8rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 99px;
  }
  .dark {
    background: var(--forest);
    color: var(--cream);
  }
  .dark p {
    color: #c4cec1;
  }
  .dark .lead {
    color: var(--cream);
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
